WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:00:38.695 --> 00:00:41.030
Let's keep those hammers working!

3
00:01:00.425 --> 00:01:02.010
Rambo!

4
00:01:04.971 --> 00:01:05.805
Let's go.

5
00:01:28.411 --> 00:01:30.163
How are you. Johnny?

6
00:01:31.164 --> 00:01:32.165
Good.

7
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:34.876
That's all.

8
00:01:38.671 --> 00:01:43.343
I'm sorry they sent you to such
a hellhole. - I've seen worse.

9
00:01:43.843 --> 00:01:45.678
Yeah. you have. haven't you...

10
00:01:46.804 --> 00:01:51.351
I told you that I'd help you
when I could. Are you interested?

11
00:01:54.771 --> 00:01:59.150
You can't possibly want
to stay here for another five years.

12
00:02:05.782 --> 00:02:10.453
In here at least I know where I stand.
- Just hear me out first.

13
00:02:12.121 --> 00:02:14.582
A covert operation
is being geared up in the Far East.

14
00:02:15.041 --> 00:02:19.712
A computer gave your name as one of
3 suitable candidates for the mission.

15
00:02:21.506 --> 00:02:24.425
Mission?
- A hunt for POWs in Vietnam.

16
00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.391
Why now? Why me?

17
00:02:33.393 --> 00:02:36.104
The prison camp you escaped from in '71
is the target area.

18
00:02:36.604 --> 00:02:41.025
No one knows that terrain better
than you. The risk factor's very high.

19
00:02:41.526 --> 00:02:44.988
You'd be temporarily reinstated in the
forces. and if the mission's successful.

20
00:02:45.446 --> 00:02:48.116
there may be a presidential pardon.

21
00:02:49.742 --> 00:02:51.828
You interested?

22
00:02:58.501 --> 00:02:59.752
Yeah.

23
00:03:00.211 --> 00:03:04.257
Good. I'll get the necessary clearance.

24
00:03:05.675 --> 00:03:09.429
The next time we meet will be in
Thailand with the special ops designate.

25
00:03:09.887 --> 00:03:11.014
Yes. sir.

26
00:03:11.472 --> 00:03:13.349
All clear?
- Yes. sir.

27
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:16.519
I want you to know I did
what I could to keep you out of here.

28
00:03:17.437 --> 00:03:18.646
I know.

29
00:03:23.276 --> 00:03:25.737
Do we get to win this time?

30
00:03:26.696 --> 00:03:28.364
This time it's up to you.

31
00:05:43.249 --> 00:05:44.917
That'll be all.

32
00:05:46.294 --> 00:05:50.882
How're you doing. Rambo? I'm Ericson.
Why don't we make it over to the hangar?

33
00:05:53.468 --> 00:05:55.887
You're the chosen one. ha?

34
00:05:56.346 --> 00:05:59.682
You made
a helluva rep for yourself in 'nam.

35
00:06:00.183 --> 00:06:02.644
I'm glad to be working with you.

36
00:06:03.102 --> 00:06:07.774
This place may not be heaven.
but at least you're out of the joint.

37
00:06:12.195 --> 00:06:13.196
He's here.

38
00:06:16.866 --> 00:06:18.201
Morning. John.

39
00:06:18.952 --> 00:06:21.829
This is Marshal Murdock.
He's in charge of special operations.

40
00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.998
Thank you. Colonel. Rambo.

41
00:06:24.499 --> 00:06:27.377
been looking forward to meeting you.
How was your trip? No problems? - No.

42
00:06:27.877 --> 00:06:30.922
Except for the damned heat. right?
I've never felt anything like it.

43
00:06:31.381 --> 00:06:33.841
Come on in.
let's get down to business.

44
00:06:35.426 --> 00:06:38.972
I was glancing over your files.

45
00:06:39.472 --> 00:06:42.267
Makes pretty interesting reading.

46
00:06:47.438 --> 00:06:52.694
Rambo. John J.. born 7.6.47. Bowie.
Arizona. of Indian-German descent.

47
00:06:53.152 --> 00:06:56.739
That's a helluva combination.
Joined the army 6.8.64.

48
00:06:57.198 --> 00:07:00.076
accepted special forces.
specialization: Light weapons.

49
00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.079
Cross-trained as medic.
Helicopter and language qualified.

50
00:07:03.538 --> 00:07:08.126
59 confirmed kills. 2 silver stars.
4 bronze. 4 Purple Hearts.

51
00:07:08.626 --> 00:07:09.961
Medal of Honor.

52
00:07:11.212 --> 00:07:16.843
You got around. didn't you?
Incredible. Rambo. you're probably aware

53
00:07:17.343 --> 00:07:20.763
that there are almost 2.500 Americans
still missing in action in SE Asia.

54
00:07:21.264 --> 00:07:25.685
Most are presumed dead. but for the
families. Congress and many Americans

55
00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:28.438
it's still an emotional issue.

56
00:07:28.938 --> 00:07:30.231
Give me something cold. please!

57
00:07:31.274 --> 00:07:35.653
Rambo. you certainly don't know
as much about me as I do you.

58
00:07:36.112 --> 00:07:39.198
I've honched with the 2nd Battalion.
3rd Marines. in Kon Tum in '66.

59
00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:43.161
I lost a lot of good men.
so I know what you and every vet feels.

60
00:07:43.661 --> 00:07:47.999
Maybe the government and certain
segments of the population didn't care.

61
00:07:48.958 --> 00:07:53.713
but my committee cares. - It needs
proof that Americans are there.

62
00:07:54.172 --> 00:07:55.590
Then we'll get 'em back.

63
00:07:56.049 --> 00:08:01.387
If there are any of our men at the POW
target camp. you're to take photos.

64
00:08:02.764 --> 00:08:05.892
Photos?
- Only photos. Under no circumstances

65
00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:10.688
are you to engage the enemy.
- I'm supposed to leave them there?

66
00:08:11.189 --> 00:08:13.983
I repeat:
Do not engage the enemy!

67
00:08:14.442 --> 00:08:18.321
The assault team led by Colonel Trautman
will handle the extraction.

68
00:08:24.869 --> 00:08:29.540
With your participation.
this mission has a better than average

69
00:08:29.999 --> 00:08:31.751
chance of succeeding.

70
00:08:33.211 --> 00:08:37.215
I'll meet you both
in the operations center in one hour.

71
00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:57.694
From Thailand across Laos
into the mountains of Vietnam.

72
00:08:58.152 --> 00:09:01.197
You'll be flying a ceiling
of 250 feet when you bail out.

73
00:09:01.698 --> 00:09:04.534
Think you can handle it?
- I'll try.

74
00:09:04.993 --> 00:09:09.247
Since you're going in solo. you'll have
to take more equipment than ever before.

75
00:09:09.706 --> 00:09:13.459
And use it!
Don't try the blood-and-guts routine.

76
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.546
Let technology do most of the work.

77
00:09:17.005 --> 00:09:21.926
Forget the war. Remember the mission.
The old Vietnam is dead.

78
00:09:22.427 --> 00:09:26.514
Sir. I'm alive.
so it's still alive. isn't it?

79
00:09:37.066 --> 00:09:40.111
You may find this hard
to believe. but all this is for you.

80
00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:42.030
Impressed?

81
00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:48.620
You'll get every modern piece of
equipment we have to ensure your safety.

82
00:09:49.078 --> 00:09:52.915
You can feel totally safe because we
have the world's most advanced weapons.

83
00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:59.589
I've always believed that the mind's
the best weapon. - Times change.

84
00:10:00.131 --> 00:10:01.341
For some people.

85
00:10:02.967 --> 00:10:04.177
Don't let me interrupt.

86
00:10:04.677 --> 00:10:07.055
Upon insertion
call in to base camp on Transat.

87
00:10:07.555 --> 00:10:13.102
Then proceed to rendezvous with your
ground contact. indigenous agent Co Bao.

88
00:10:13.561 --> 00:10:15.605
Is he listening?

89
00:10:16.064 --> 00:10:18.775
Indigenous agent Co Bao.

90
00:10:26.199 --> 00:10:27.492
Colonel!

91
00:10:28.701 --> 00:10:30.787
Are you sure he's not unbalanced?

92
00:10:31.287 --> 00:10:36.167
What if he cracks under the pressure
in that hell? - Pressure?

93
00:10:37.126 --> 00:10:39.587
Rambo is the best combat vet
I've ever seen.

94
00:10:40.046 --> 00:10:44.259
A pure fighting machine with only
a desire to win a war someone else lost.

95
00:10:44.717 --> 00:10:49.889
If winning means he has to die.
he'll die. No fear. no regrets.

96
00:10:51.516 --> 00:10:53.184
And one more thing:

97
00:10:53.685 --> 00:10:57.563
What you call "hell". he calls home.

98
00:11:01.276 --> 00:11:03.528
Stand by! Start A.P.U.!

99
00:11:27.552 --> 00:11:29.262
D minus 20.

100
00:12:01.502 --> 00:12:02.879
D minus 5.

101
00:12:18.853 --> 00:12:23.942
You've got 36 hours to get in and out.
So don't stop to smell the roses. okay?

102
00:12:24.901 --> 00:12:30.865
If you run into trouble. try to get
to the hilltop extraction site.

103
00:12:36.663 --> 00:12:38.331
Good luck. son.
- Thanks.

104
00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.333
Ready to roll.

105
00:12:42.961 --> 00:12:47.340
Murdock said he'd been
with the 2nd Battalion in Kon Tum '66.

106
00:12:48.675 --> 00:12:51.094
The 2nd Battalion was at Kud Sank.

107
00:12:52.971 --> 00:12:54.889
You're the only one that I trust.

108
00:13:36.723 --> 00:13:40.852
Think he'll find someone?
- POWs? Doubtful.

109
00:13:41.311 --> 00:13:45.898
But there are people to satisfy.
questions that have to be answered.

110
00:13:46.399 --> 00:13:49.736
You don't sound too emotional about it.
- It wasn't my war. Colonel.

111
00:13:50.194 --> 00:13:52.655
I'm here to clean up the mess.

112
00:14:36.157 --> 00:14:37.867
K-Wok 2-5 is raft.

113
00:14:38.368 --> 00:14:39.953
They're holding timeline.

114
00:14:40.453 --> 00:14:42.789
Affirmative. Wolf Den. Over.

115
00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.242
We're back in the badlands. my man.

116
00:15:20.368 --> 00:15:22.078
Stand by your position!

117
00:15:22.578 --> 00:15:25.665
Insertion in 15 seconds.
- Partytime!

118
00:15:38.928 --> 00:15:39.929
5 seconds.

119
00:15:58.448 --> 00:16:01.034
What's happening?
- He's hung up!

120
00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.413
He'll be torn apart!

121
00:16:07.415 --> 00:16:10.793
He's hung up! - What do you mean he's
hung up? - He's being dragged!

122
00:16:13.838 --> 00:16:15.798
Cut him loose!
- I can't free him!

123
00:16:37.403 --> 00:16:40.573
Abort the mission!
- That'll kill him! He'll be torn apart!

124
00:16:44.035 --> 00:16:45.954
He's cutting away his equipment.

125
00:16:57.632 --> 00:16:59.217
He's out!

126
00:16:59.717 --> 00:17:03.888
Here is Dragonfly 1. Do you read me?
- Dragonfly 1. I read you.

127
00:17:04.389 --> 00:17:07.934
Any visual bearing by flares?
- Negative. We didn't see anything.

128
00:17:15.692 --> 00:17:21.781
Maybe it's best to abort
the mission now. Who could survive that?

129
00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.992
He deserves the benefit of the doubt.

130
00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:28.997
He's got 36 hours to complete the
mission and reach the extraction point.

131
00:17:29.455 --> 00:17:32.375
We owe him that.
- Of course we do.

132
00:17:33.334 --> 00:17:38.172
But understand something:
In 36 hours we pull out.

133
00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:23.528
Rambo!

134
00:19:37.875 --> 00:19:40.044
You did not expect a woman. no?

135
00:19:42.422 --> 00:19:44.048
We'd better go.

136
00:19:46.884 --> 00:19:51.306
We go to river.
How come you so late?

137
00:19:51.764 --> 00:19:53.308
I was hung up.

138
00:19:59.105 --> 00:20:03.276
I have arranged boat to take us
down river. Old ways not safe.

139
00:20:03.735 --> 00:20:07.739
You come a long way. Rambo.
to see empty camp.

140
00:21:00.625 --> 00:21:02.085
You're using pirates?

141
00:21:02.585 --> 00:21:07.715
Best way down river.
Not get army suspicious.

142
00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:29.964
What about patrol boats?

143
00:22:51.152 --> 00:22:52.528
Russian.

144
00:23:20.473 --> 00:23:21.182
Rambo.

145
00:23:22.433 --> 00:23:24.644
want to eat?

146
00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:27.855
Maybe later.

147
00:23:36.656 --> 00:23:38.324
How you get into this?

148
00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:44.247
It's a long story.
- Long trip.

149
00:23:47.208 --> 00:23:50.461
After I left the special forces.

150
00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:55.216
I moved around a lot.
- Why you leave army?

151
00:23:55.717 --> 00:23:56.884
I...

152
00:23:58.595 --> 00:24:00.930
...came back to the States

153
00:24:01.431 --> 00:24:03.683
and found another war going on.

154
00:24:05.018 --> 00:24:07.145
What war?

155
00:24:08.062 --> 00:24:09.897
Kind of like a quiet war.

156
00:24:11.983 --> 00:24:17.864
A war against the soldiers returning.
The kind of war you don't win.

157
00:24:23.995 --> 00:24:26.998
It's my problem.
How did you get into it?

158
00:24:28.625 --> 00:24:32.670
My father
worked for intelligence agency.

159
00:24:33.796 --> 00:24:37.425
He killed. and I take his place.

160
00:24:37.926 --> 00:24:39.385
There's too much death here.

161
00:24:40.386 --> 00:24:41.554
Death everywhere.

162
00:24:45.808 --> 00:24:47.310
I just want to live.

163
00:24:51.105 --> 00:24:55.109
Maybe go America. Live the quiet life.

164
00:24:58.821 --> 00:25:00.740
What you want?

165
00:25:02.951 --> 00:25:05.620
To win. To survive.

166
00:25:07.622 --> 00:25:11.292
Not so easy to survive. Still war here.

167
00:25:11.793 --> 00:25:15.505
To survive a war.
you've got to become war.

168
00:25:16.005 --> 00:25:19.425
That why they pick you?
Because you like to fight?

169
00:25:24.472 --> 00:25:26.391
I am expendable.

170
00:25:29.143 --> 00:25:30.895
What mean "expendable"?

171
00:25:33.273 --> 00:25:34.315
It's like

172
00:25:34.816 --> 00:25:40.697
someone invites you to a party
and you don't show up.

173
00:25:41.155 --> 00:25:43.157
and it doesn't really matter.

174
00:25:50.123 --> 00:25:51.583
What's this?

175
00:25:52.834 --> 00:25:55.003
It bring me good luck.

176
00:25:56.671 --> 00:25:58.965
What bring you good luck?

177
00:26:06.598 --> 00:26:08.558
I guess this.

178
00:26:15.106 --> 00:26:18.943
No further reports. - I want to go up
with the extraction team at dawn.

179
00:26:19.402 --> 00:26:20.945
Denied.
- Denied?

180
00:26:21.446 --> 00:26:24.115
It's an unnecessary risk.
- We have a schedule to keep.

181
00:26:24.574 --> 00:26:26.993
We don't even know if he's alive.
- Unlikely.

182
00:26:27.452 --> 00:26:29.787
You said we'd go through as planned.

183
00:26:31.456 --> 00:26:35.251
Okay. if you
want to go through with it. we will.

184
00:26:35.752 --> 00:26:38.004
The Colonel's
gonna be joining the extraction team.

185
00:26:41.174 --> 00:26:43.009
You're a damned good man. Trautman.

186
00:27:40.441 --> 00:27:42.860
See? Camp empty.

187
00:27:43.987 --> 00:27:45.989
We move closer.

188
00:28:30.491 --> 00:28:32.952
Cyclo-girl whore from village.

189
00:28:37.457 --> 00:28:38.583
Come on!

190
00:28:54.474 --> 00:28:57.685
What is it?
- A bow. No sound.

191
00:29:04.567 --> 00:29:09.072
You not going in there.
You're supposed to only take pictures.

192
00:29:09.572 --> 00:29:10.782
What about orders?

193
00:29:11.783 --> 00:29:13.201
No more orders. Co.

194
00:32:56.925 --> 00:32:58.384
I've come to get you out.

195
00:33:00.053 --> 00:33:01.679
Don't talk.

196
00:33:30.166 --> 00:33:33.503
There are others.
- I'll be back.

197
00:35:13.394 --> 00:35:14.270
Everything okay?

198
00:35:15.063 --> 00:35:16.606
Let's go!

199
00:35:49.973 --> 00:35:51.724
You have clearance.

200
00:35:52.183 --> 00:35:54.269
Minus one hour to extraction.

201
00:35:54.727 --> 00:35:57.772
I hope for his sake
we're not just wasting fuel.

202
00:35:58.273 --> 00:36:00.275
Let's get moving.

203
00:36:22.338 --> 00:36:24.424
A good thing you came when you did.

204
00:36:24.924 --> 00:36:26.217
Why is that?

205
00:36:26.926 --> 00:36:30.638
They move us around a lot. Because
of the crops. Only been there a week.

206
00:36:31.306 --> 00:36:36.561
When were you last in that camp?
- A year. What year is it. anyway?

207
00:36:37.353 --> 00:36:38.938
1985.

208
00:36:42.817 --> 00:36:45.278
Camp supposed to be empty.

209
00:36:45.945 --> 00:36:47.572
Yes. supposed to be.

210
00:37:20.647 --> 00:37:24.025
Landing zone a mile up river.

211
00:38:24.669 --> 00:38:27.255
What has happened?
- We've been sold out.

212
00:38:29.007 --> 00:38:30.133
You bastard!

213
00:39:06.336 --> 00:39:09.172
Right. jump!
- I fight!

214
00:39:09.672 --> 00:39:10.965
Jump! Go on!

215
00:40:06.688 --> 00:40:08.189
The gunboat!

216
00:40:26.249 --> 00:40:27.125
Jump!

217
00:40:39.637 --> 00:40:41.514
You made it. Rambo!

218
00:40:49.772 --> 00:40:50.940
Come on.

219
00:41:15.673 --> 00:41:18.217
Take this. We go on from here.

220
00:41:19.427 --> 00:41:22.096
Better I stay on to end.
- This is the end.

221
00:41:23.806 --> 00:41:24.599
Come on.

222
00:41:26.100 --> 00:41:27.143
Rambo!

223
00:41:28.645 --> 00:41:30.647
You not expendable.

224
00:41:54.128 --> 00:41:56.256
Colonel. 3 minutes.

225
00:43:08.786 --> 00:43:10.121
That's Rambo!

226
00:43:16.753 --> 00:43:18.129
Christ. he's found one!

227
00:43:48.618 --> 00:43:50.787
Rambo's found one of ours!

228
00:43:51.913 --> 00:43:56.626
The ground crew has what appears to be
an American POW with him.

229
00:43:57.627 --> 00:44:00.922
What did you say?
- They've got one of ours.

230
00:44:02.048 --> 00:44:04.592
Yellow alert!
Meyers. Harrison. Goddell!

231
00:44:05.093 --> 00:44:08.137
Everybody out! Move!

232
00:44:08.596 --> 00:44:10.890
Go to your COMINT frequency!
Give me the mike!

233
00:44:13.726 --> 00:44:17.939
Dragonfly. here is Coach 1.
This is a priority order.

234
00:44:19.649 --> 00:44:21.109
Come on!

235
00:44:24.404 --> 00:44:27.657
Abort the operation immediately!

236
00:44:28.157 --> 00:44:31.619
This is a recall. Confirm. Over.
- Say it again. Coach 1.

237
00:44:32.036 --> 00:44:33.663
Abort the operation!

238
00:44:34.998 --> 00:44:38.960
I've been ordered to abort.
- But we've got them in sight!

239
00:44:39.460 --> 00:44:41.045
Murdock. do you read?

240
00:44:45.049 --> 00:44:47.927
We're going down.
- You're not going anywhere.

241
00:44:51.306 --> 00:44:55.310
You damned mercenaries!
Those are our men down there!

242
00:44:56.311 --> 00:44:59.647
No. your men. Don't be a hero.

243
00:45:06.654 --> 00:45:07.780
Colonel!

244
00:45:08.281 --> 00:45:09.741
Down!

245
00:45:50.823 --> 00:45:53.952
What are you doing?
Do you know what the hell you've done?

246
00:45:54.410 --> 00:45:56.829
Don't act so innocent. Colonel.

247
00:45:57.330 --> 00:45:59.999
You had your suspicions.
which makes you a sort of accessory.

248
00:46:00.458 --> 00:46:03.127
Don't ever
count me with you and your scum!

249
00:46:03.628 --> 00:46:07.799
It was a lie. wasn't it.
Like the whole damned war. It was a lie.

250
00:46:08.299 --> 00:46:09.842
What are you talking about?

251
00:46:10.343 --> 00:46:13.012
That camp was supposed to be empty.

252
00:46:14.055 --> 00:46:18.601
Rambo goes in. finds no POWs.
Congress buys it. case closed.

253
00:46:19.102 --> 00:46:24.440
And if he happens to get caught.
nobody knows except you.

254
00:46:24.899 --> 00:46:27.485
Who the hell
do you think you're talking to?

255
00:46:27.986 --> 00:46:33.992
A stinking bureaucrat who's trying to
cover his ass. - A nation's!

256
00:46:34.450 --> 00:46:38.913
Besides. it was your hero's fault. If
he had done what he was meant to do.

257
00:46:39.414 --> 00:46:43.876
we'd be out of this clean and simple.
He was just supposed to take pictures.

258
00:46:44.335 --> 00:46:48.548
And if those pictures showed something.
they'd have been lost.

259
00:46:49.007 --> 00:46:51.509
You still don't understand
what this is all about.

260
00:46:52.010 --> 00:46:54.554
Same as always: Money.

261
00:46:55.054 --> 00:46:58.182
In '72 we were supposed to pay the Cong
4.5 billion in war reparation.

262
00:46:58.683 --> 00:47:01.269
We reneged. they kept the POWs.

263
00:47:01.728 --> 00:47:04.480
And you're doing the same thing
all over again.

264
00:47:04.981 --> 00:47:06.441
What would you do?

265
00:47:06.899 --> 00:47:11.529
Pay ransom for our men and finance
the war effort against our allies?

266
00:47:11.988 --> 00:47:14.657
And if some burnt-out POW
shows up on the 6 o'clock news?

267
00:47:15.116 --> 00:47:19.996
Do you want to start the war over again
and bomb Hanoi?

268
00:47:20.455 --> 00:47:26.419
You think the Senate's going to pay
billions for a few forgotten ghosts?

269
00:47:26.920 --> 00:47:30.632
For men! Men who fought
for their country! - That's enough!

270
00:47:32.091 --> 00:47:36.804
Trautman. I'm going to forget
this conversation ever took place.

271
00:47:38.473 --> 00:47:41.142
You bastard!
- And if I were you.

272
00:47:41.643 --> 00:47:46.397
I'd not make the mistake of bringing it
up again. - You're making the mistake.

273
00:47:46.856 --> 00:47:48.358
Yes? What mistake?

274
00:47:49.692 --> 00:47:51.069
Rambo.

275
00:48:50.837 --> 00:48:53.548
Damned Russian bastards.

276
00:49:18.156 --> 00:49:19.991
He's dead now.

277
00:49:30.126 --> 00:49:31.753
Bring him up!

278
00:49:51.147 --> 00:49:52.899
The knife!

279
00:49:53.399 --> 00:49:56.194
These people
are so vulgar in their methods!

280
00:49:57.028 --> 00:49:59.572
They lack compassion.

281
00:50:02.283 --> 00:50:05.703
I'm Lieutenant-Colonel Podovski.

282
00:50:07.330 --> 00:50:09.707
I do not know who you are yet.

283
00:50:10.208 --> 00:50:12.001
but I will.

284
00:50:12.460 --> 00:50:14.003
Take him and clean him up.

285
00:50:48.830 --> 00:50:50.290
That's all.

286
00:50:50.748 --> 00:50:54.586
Thank you. Captain Vinh.
Leave one guard. please.

287
00:50:59.299 --> 00:51:02.552
I see you are no stranger to pain.

288
00:51:03.011 --> 00:51:06.556
Perhaps you have been
among my Vietnamese comrades before?

289
00:51:09.559 --> 00:51:10.768
No answer?

290
00:51:11.936 --> 00:51:14.355
Do you wish to give your name?

291
00:51:14.856 --> 00:51:18.109
What possible harm can that cause?

292
00:51:21.154 --> 00:51:23.907
Pride is a poor substitute
for intelligence.

293
00:51:24.782 --> 00:51:28.161
What you must understand
is that we must interrogate you.

294
00:51:30.830 --> 00:51:34.834
For Sergeant Yushin you're a piece
of meat. a laboratory experiment.

295
00:51:35.293 --> 00:51:38.796
But for me you are a comrade.
similar to myself.

296
00:51:39.297 --> 00:51:42.634
just opposed by an act of fate.

297
00:51:44.218 --> 00:51:46.304
I know you were trying

298
00:51:46.763 --> 00:51:51.184
to facilitate the release
of war criminals. I can appreciate this.

299
00:51:52.268 --> 00:51:56.314
But this incident. your capture. is...

300
00:51:58.316 --> 00:51:59.525
...embarrassing.

301
00:52:00.193 --> 00:52:02.028
We must have an explanation.

302
00:52:02.487 --> 00:52:08.534
Radio your HQ and say that
you have been captured and condemned

303
00:52:09.035 --> 00:52:15.333
for espionage. and that attempts like
these should not be made in the future.

304
00:52:15.833 --> 00:52:20.463
or they
will meet with the same fate as you.

305
00:52:29.806 --> 00:52:31.307
Fuck you!

306
00:52:34.102 --> 00:52:37.438
You wish to test your strength... Good.

307
00:52:42.026 --> 00:52:43.611
Yushin!

308
00:53:43.630 --> 00:53:45.381
Comrade. here is something

309
00:53:45.882 --> 00:53:49.010
that might be of interest to you:

310
00:53:49.510 --> 00:53:53.264
A transcript of the conversation
between your helicopter pilot

311
00:53:53.765 --> 00:53:57.101
and his commander that we intercepted.

312
00:53:58.561 --> 00:54:02.899
"Dragonfly" and "Wolf's Den"...
Colorful names.

313
00:54:03.816 --> 00:54:04.901
Here we are:

314
00:54:05.360 --> 00:54:12.408
"We have them in sight". And the reply:
"Abort the operation immediately. "

315
00:54:13.826 --> 00:54:18.206
"This is a recall. Confirm. Over. "

316
00:54:19.374 --> 00:54:24.003
It seems you were abandoned
by direct command.

317
00:54:24.504 --> 00:54:27.757
And these are the people
you protect with your pain!

318
00:54:28.591 --> 00:54:30.843
Increase the voltage.

319
00:54:32.178 --> 00:54:36.182
You may scream. There is no shame.

320
00:55:07.005 --> 00:55:09.716
You are strong! Very strong!

321
00:55:10.174 --> 00:55:12.010
The strongest so far.

322
00:55:12.760 --> 00:55:16.180
But you're nearly dead. Poor waif.

323
00:55:16.764 --> 00:55:20.059
Make the radio call.

324
00:55:44.709 --> 00:55:47.754
To talk. to obey
would be so much easier.

325
00:56:02.685 --> 00:56:05.939
Yushin
has a memento for you of this day.

326
00:56:27.794 --> 00:56:30.421
Put it in his eye.

327
00:56:36.886 --> 00:56:41.182
If your own life
means nothing to you. perhaps his does.

328
00:56:41.683 --> 00:56:45.353
Don't tell them anything!
- You will talk.

329
00:56:55.363 --> 00:56:56.698
Yes?

330
00:57:32.233 --> 00:57:33.693
Don't do it!

331
00:57:35.945 --> 00:57:37.363
Do it

332
00:57:37.864 --> 00:57:39.282
now!

333
00:58:08.102 --> 00:58:11.147
Two-two-zero-five-six...

334
00:58:12.023 --> 00:58:14.275
Lone Wolf receive.

335
00:58:15.818 --> 00:58:18.321
This is Lone Wolf...

336
00:58:19.197 --> 00:58:23.368
Lone Wolf. this is Wolf's Den.
Transmit location and status.

337
00:58:23.868 --> 00:58:26.871
What is it?
- It's Rambo. Sir.

338
00:58:27.997 --> 00:58:31.042
We read you.
Lone Wolf. What is your position? Over.

339
00:58:32.669 --> 00:58:35.505
I say again:
What is your position? Over.

340
00:58:37.006 --> 00:58:40.802
Your friend dies if you do not answer.

341
00:58:42.679 --> 00:58:44.764
This is Trautman. Where are you?

342
00:58:49.602 --> 00:58:50.937
Come in!

343
00:58:59.988 --> 00:59:00.947
Murdock...

344
00:59:02.448 --> 00:59:03.992
He's here.

345
00:59:08.371 --> 00:59:10.790
Rambo. we're glad you're alive.

346
00:59:11.583 --> 00:59:15.920
Where are you? Give us your position.
and we'll come to pick you up.

347
00:59:24.804 --> 00:59:25.847
Murdock...

348
00:59:29.267 --> 00:59:31.185
I'm coming to get you!

349
01:01:53.536 --> 01:01:54.787
Duck!

350
01:03:00.103 --> 01:03:01.312
This way.

351
01:03:39.392 --> 01:03:41.603
We safe for now.

352
01:03:46.149 --> 01:03:50.486
You look like hell. Rambo.
- Tough night.

353
01:03:51.571 --> 01:03:53.698
Maybe need this.

354
01:03:56.200 --> 01:03:59.287
You hurt bad.
- It's alright.

355
01:04:06.419 --> 01:04:07.587
Listen...

356
01:04:08.504 --> 01:04:11.591
What you did back there...

357
01:04:12.091 --> 01:04:14.385
...I won't forget it.

358
01:04:16.054 --> 01:04:17.096
Thanks.

359
01:04:19.807 --> 01:04:21.142
What you do now?

360
01:04:21.601 --> 01:04:24.020
Try get across through Thailand?

361
01:04:24.520 --> 01:04:27.231
Yeah.
- Then go America?

362
01:04:34.322 --> 01:04:36.407
You take me with you?

363
01:04:47.627 --> 01:04:49.128
You take me?

364
01:04:51.506 --> 01:04:52.465
Yeah.

365
01:04:55.635 --> 01:04:57.512
I think you make good choice.

366
01:05:00.515 --> 01:05:02.100
We go?
- Let's go.

367
01:05:39.637 --> 01:05:41.222
You alright?

368
01:05:54.903 --> 01:05:57.655
You... not... forget... me.

369
01:05:58.114 --> 01:05:59.365
No.

370
01:06:18.092 --> 01:06:20.219
I want the rescue team
ready to go in one hour.

371
01:06:20.678 --> 01:06:26.684
You're risking everything. Do you think
one man's worth all that? - Yes.

372
01:06:27.143 --> 01:06:31.397
I order you to withdraw.
- I'll go over your head.

373
01:06:31.898 --> 01:06:36.236
You don't seem to understand that I'm
in charge here. You're just a tool.

374
01:06:37.612 --> 01:06:40.073
We're the machine.

375
01:06:40.573 --> 01:06:42.909
He's not to leave the base.

376
01:06:47.622 --> 01:06:52.335
He never had a chance. did he?
- Like you said: He went home.

377
01:21:07.065 --> 01:21:08.149
Get back.

378
01:21:12.904 --> 01:21:15.490
Come on! To the chopper!

379
01:21:15.949 --> 01:21:17.075
Move!

380
01:21:17.575 --> 01:21:19.661
To the chopper!

381
01:21:36.386 --> 01:21:37.887
Move!

382
01:22:10.920 --> 01:22:12.046
You guys made it!

383
01:22:50.084 --> 01:22:52.045
Chopper on your tail!

384
01:22:53.671 --> 01:22:55.131
Hang on!

385
01:24:24.262 --> 01:24:25.305
Hold on!

386
01:24:32.645 --> 01:24:33.897
Fire in the tail!

387
01:26:38.229 --> 01:26:40.315
Lone Wolf calling Wolf's Den. Over.

388
01:26:41.816 --> 01:26:45.069
Lone Wolf calling Wolf's Den. Over.

389
01:26:45.778 --> 01:26:49.449
Wolf's Den.
this is Lone wolf. do you read?

390
01:26:52.201 --> 01:26:53.494
We hear you. Lone Wolf. Over.

391
01:26:53.953 --> 01:26:58.708
Prepare for emergency landing.
Arriving with American POWs.

392
01:27:10.970 --> 01:27:15.099
You heard. Prepare for landing of POWs!

393
01:28:31.926 --> 01:28:34.053
Glad you made it.

394
01:29:45.500 --> 01:29:48.044
Rambo. I don't make the orders.

395
01:29:48.544 --> 01:29:50.672
I take them. just like you.

396
01:29:54.926 --> 01:29:58.805
I swear to God I didn't know
it was supposed to happen like this.

397
01:29:59.264 --> 01:30:02.100
It was just supposed
to be another assignment.

398
01:30:09.315 --> 01:30:10.358
Mission...

399
01:30:11.943 --> 01:30:13.653
...accomplished!

400
01:30:20.994 --> 01:30:23.329
You know there are more men out there.

401
01:30:24.080 --> 01:30:25.915
You know where they are.

402
01:30:28.209 --> 01:30:31.838
Find them. or I'll find you!

403
01:30:56.821 --> 01:30:58.615
Where are you going?

404
01:30:59.115 --> 01:31:00.783
I don't know.

405
01:31:02.452 --> 01:31:05.496
You'll get
a second Medal of Honor for this.

406
01:31:13.421 --> 01:31:18.009
They should give it to them.
They deserve it more.

407
01:31:19.344 --> 01:31:22.847
You can't keep running. John.
You're free now.

408
01:31:23.348 --> 01:31:25.475
Come back to us.

409
01:31:26.684 --> 01:31:28.436
Back to what?

410
01:31:29.562 --> 01:31:32.106
My friends died here.

411
01:31:33.191 --> 01:31:35.401
and part of me died here.

412
01:31:36.486 --> 01:31:42.033
The war may have been wrong.
but don't hate your country for it.

413
01:31:43.159 --> 01:31:44.118
Hate it?

414
01:31:45.370 --> 01:31:47.038
I'd die for it!

415
01:31:48.790 --> 01:31:50.833
What is it you want?

416
01:31:56.047 --> 01:31:57.882
I want

417
01:32:00.051 --> 01:32:02.053
what they want.

418
01:32:02.512 --> 01:32:05.723
and every other guy who came out here

419
01:32:06.224 --> 01:32:10.478
and spilt his guts
and gave everything he had:

420
01:32:12.480 --> 01:32:14.857
For our country to love us

421
01:32:15.358 --> 01:32:17.443
as much as we love it.

422
01:32:20.154 --> 01:32:21.906
That's what I want.

423
01:32:28.538 --> 01:32:32.333
How will you live. John?
- Day by day.

424
01:32:33.305 --> 01:33:33.493
